          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"counterterms-retain-uv-finite-integrals\">Counterterms retain UV-finite integrals</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">A mass insertion produces a UV-finite one-loop integral, but its coefficient contains a renormalization pole. Dropping that integral would lose part of the two-loop counterterm. Keep the entire zeroth-order Taylor coefficient and reduce both doubled and tripled tadpoles with the parametric IBP recurrence.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">The scalar mass and logarithms cancel between bare graphs and counterterm insertions. The generated local vertex contains both the coupling and field renormalization constants; the previously computed field constant is required to determine <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(Z_g||)</marimo-tex>.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "PKri",
      "code_hash": "15bdfc9a492222b2f71fb43fb543d708",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/html": "<div style='display: flex;flex: 1;flex-direction: column;justify-content: flex-start;align-items: normal;flex-wrap: nowrap;gap: 0.5rem'><span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>Generated one-loop counterterm integral combination</strong></span></span><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap; margin: 0;\">-3\u00b7M\u00b7field1\u00b7J<span style=\"color: rgb(0, 95, 175)\">(</span>3<span style=\"color: rgb(0, 95, 175)\">)</span><span style=\"color: rgb(205, 205, 0)\">-</span>3\u00b7field1\u00b7J<span style=\"color: rgb(0, 95, 175)\">(</span>2<span style=\"color: rgb(0, 95, 175)\">)</span><span style=\"color: rgb(205, 205, 0)\">+</span>6\u00b7<span style=\"color: rgb(128, 128, 128)\">(</span>field1+1/2\u00b7vertex1<span style=\"color: rgb(128, 128, 128)\">)</span>\u00b7J<span style=\"color: rgb(0, 95, 175)\">(</span>2<span style=\"color: rgb(0, 95, 175)\">)</span><span style=\"color: rgb(205, 205, 0)\">+</span>3\u00b7<span style=\"color: rgb(128, 128, 128)\">(</span>M\u00b7field1+M\u00b7mass1<span style=\"color: rgb(128, 128, 128)\">)</span>\u00b7J<span style=\"color: rgb(0, 95, 175)\">(</span>3<span style=\"color: rgb(0, 95, 175)\">)</span></div><span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>Tripled-tadpole recurrence</strong></span></span><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap; margin: 0;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(128, 128, 128)\">(</span>1/4\u00b7d/M-1/M<span style=\"color: rgb(128, 128, 128)\">)</span>\u00b7<span style=\"color: rgb(128, 128, 128)\">(</span>1/2\u00b7d/M-1/M<span style=\"color: rgb(128, 128, 128)\">)</span>\u00b7J<span style=\"color: rgb(0, 95, 175)\">(</span>1<span style=\"color: rgb(0, 95, 175)\">)</span></div><span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>One-loop counterterm poles</strong></span></span><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap; margin: 0;\">-3/4/eps<span style=\"color: rgb(205, 205, 0)\">-</span>9/2\u00b7Lm/eps<span style=\"color: rgb(205, 205, 0)\">+</span>9/2\u00b7L4pi/eps<span style=\"color: rgb(205, 205, 0)\">+</span>9/2/eps\u00b2</div><span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>Pole from the UV-finite mass insertion</strong></span></span><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap; margin: 0;\">-3/4/eps</div><span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>Sum before local subtraction</strong></span></span><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap; margin: 0;\">-3/2/eps<span style=\"color: rgb(205, 205, 0)\">+</span>9/4/eps\u00b2</div><span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>Generated local counterterm matrix</strong></span></span><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap; margin: 0;\">[[-1]]</div><span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>Coupling renormalization</strong></span></span><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap; margin: 0;\">1<span style=\"color: rgb(205, 205, 0)\">+</span>3/32\u00b7g/<span style=\"color: rgb(128, 128, 128)\">(</span><span style=\"color: rgb(205, 0, 205)\">\ud835\udf0b</span>\u00b2\u00b7eps<span style=\"color: rgb(128, 128, 128)\">)</span><span style=\"color: rgb(205, 205, 0)\">-</span>17/3072\u00b7g\u00b2/<span style=\"color: rgb(128, 128, 128)\">(</span><span style=\"color: rgb(205, 0, 205)\">\ud835\udf0b</span>\u2074\u00b7eps<span style=\"color: rgb(128, 128, 128)\">)</span><span style=\"color: rgb(205, 205, 0)\">+</span>9/1024\u00b7g\u00b2/<span style=\"color: rgb(128, 128, 128)\">(</span><span style=\"color: rgb(205, 0, 205)\">\ud835\udf0b</span>\u2074\u00b7eps\u00b2<span style=\"color: rgb(128, 128, 128)\">)</span></div><span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\">All poles cancel exactly after inserting the solved coupling constant.</span></span></div>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
